# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository, regardless of platform or
# local core.autocrlf. Same rationale as the destined-module repo's
# .gitattributes: a zip round-trip or a second machine's autocrlf setting
# can flip every source file's line endings, producing a phantom whole-file
# diff that only vanishes under --ignore-cr-at-eol. That's poison for a
# workflow built on diff-reading, and will recur with any second machine,
# contributor, or future work.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary declarations so a zip round-trip or a different machine's
# autocrlf setting can never mangle these — `text=auto`'s content-sniffing
# heuristic is usually right, but "usually" is exactly the gap this file
# exists to close.
*.png            binary
*.webp           binary
*.jpg            binary
*.jpeg           binary
*.pdf            binary
